      },
      "lineNbr": 27,
      "author": {
        "id": 1380243
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-08T10:59:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not, I didn\u0027t realise that that was necessary. Why is this extra step required? However, `set_requesting_sid` isn\u0027t currently part of the public API exposed for AIDL interfaces. Should it be? Or should the AIDL codegen automatically call it as needed? Either way, it should be a separate change.",
      "parentUuid": "cb158d7a_e080878d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 27,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 27,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "b8f1e9608fa330e3f466ef0d6459d03b6d4de676",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "119af74f_ffe7c34b",
        "filename": "virtmanager/aidl/android/system/virtmanager/VirtualMachineDebugInfo.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 27,
      "author": {
        "id": 1120458
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-12T22:01:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is a performance cost associated with looking up the SIDs w/ the proper locks taken, so it must be enabled conditionally per binder, rather than always being available.\n\nThis API should be exposed. AIDL can\u0027t know to call it now because there is no annotation or other signal exposing when this should be used - in fact, in general, there can be no such annotation because usage of this may be independent from interface ownership, and the same interface may theoretically be implemented with and without this (and in a secure way).",
      "parentUuid": "a14f0bce_18223ced",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 27,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 27,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "b8f1e9608fa330e3f466ef0d6459d03b6d4de676",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
